When we have multiple versions of patch series, earlier versions clog up
my notmuch view.

I would like to introduce "Overcome by" trailer processing. The idea is
that when posting v2 of a patch, a reply can also be sent to the first
email of the v1 series. It would have a trailer section, and if one of
the trailers is: "Overcome by: id:<msgid>" then it indicates that that
thread has been overcome. It would receive an overcome notmuch tag,
which I would exclude from view.

Additionally I want "Approved by" and "Rejected by" at the commit and
thread level.

Though I realize now I'm probably proposing a workflow similar to what
LKML, OpenBSD, Postgres projects do.

So, research how they track versions of patch series, and how they
indicate states like approved, rejected, etc. Report on what you find so
that we can develop a workflow.

Again a goal of this workflow is to have the current state of the list
be derivable from the contents of the list. So I won't tag things as
overcome or accepted - those need to be derived from the
contents. Supporting trailers - or a similar mechanism - lets me add
metadata to emails after the fact.
